  "manual_audits": {
    "finite_core": "Root, braid and arithmetic checked explicit tail centralizers, Fourier invariants, restriction to the reducing canonical subspace, the lazy Kazhdan gap, exact distance one, diagonalization in tracial ultraproducts, the literal finite trace expansion, and the essential varying-depth boundary. Property (T) is transported from rank four using the cited graph prerequisites.",
    "internal_shift": "Braid and root checked ring generation by units, the exact finite scalar centralizer, Fourier fixed spaces, conditional expectation in every finite extension, and the one-coordinate distance-one witness. No inner implementation of the shift or identification of coordinate and limiting commutants is assumed.",
    "dimension_and_distortion": "Arithmetic, braid and root checked aggregate Fourier Parseval, separate spectral rounding, rank integrality, the constants and literal native subgroup conjugacy. Arithmetic and root also checked projective two-transitivity, growing irreducible degree, CRT surjectivity, canonical fixed-word traces, both commutant weight families, and persistence under central deletion.",
    "seven_cell": "Charge and root reviewed the seven-cell finite core, the diagonal Thompson embedding, the exact one-equation completion criterion, and the obstruction when the remaining involution fixes the moved region. Charge, braid and root separately checked fixed-point prefix-length germs, preservation of eventual-tail classes, reversibility and square-root obstructions, and the native length-72 square row. These are written arguments, not additional claims about what the prefix replay checks. No completed involution is claimed."
  },
  "verification_boundary": "Cairn checks graph structure and dependency closure, not mathematical proof correctness. The prefix replay verifies only its explicitly named exact identities. The written arguments have separate manual reviews and no new Lean verification. The growing dimension packet is not a fixed-packet uniform gap; fixed-core separation does not rule out all moving-depth approximations. Fixed-germ obstructions exclude the prescribed two-copy diagonal architectures after imposing the true native square row; they do not exclude arbitrary Thompson embeddings or prove that row independent of the eight imposed relations. Passing the necessary germ tests in a larger architecture is not a completion. The Thompson completion equation is unsolved and hyperlinearity of Thompson V is not assumed. The headline existence goal remains open.",
